---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const APP_URL = "https://trading.onquantex.com";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="AI Hub"
  description="How Quantex's AI reads the market and helps you set up a Grid, DCA, or Momentum bot."
>
  <section class="qx-ai-hero">
    <div class="qx-container">
      <span class="qx-eyebrow">AI Hub</span>
      <h1>The AI reads the market before you deploy a bot</h1>
      <p class="qx-lead">
        Not an autopilot that trades on its own, a second opinion. It
        looks at what the market's doing right now and hands you a read
        on it, in plain language, before you commit to a strategy.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="qx-section">
    <div class="qx-container qx-prose">
      <h2>What it actually looks at</h2>
      <p>
        For whichever pair you're setting a bot up on, it pulls recent
        price action and volatility across a few timeframes, the same
        chart you'd be squinting at yourself, just checked systematically
        instead of by eye. It's not reading news sentiment or making a
        prediction about tomorrow, it's describing what the chart is
        doing right now.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="qx-section qx-section-alt">
    <div class="qx-container qx-prose">
      <h2>A verdict, not a black box</h2>
      <p>
        You get a straightforward tag, bullish or bearish, and a reasoning
        card explaining why it landed there: what it saw in the price
        action that led to that read. Nothing about it is a hidden score
        you're asked to just trust, you can see the reasoning and decide
        for yourself whether you agree with it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="qx-section">
    <div class="qx-container qx-prose">
      <h2>Auto-suggested starting parameters</h2>
      <p>
        Once you've seen the read, you can let it auto-fill a sensible
        starting configuration, a price range for a Grid bot, an interval
        for DCA, based on that same analysis, instead of staring at a
        blank form guessing at numbers. It's a starting point, not a
        final answer: every field it fills in is still yours to edit
        before you deploy anything.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="qx-section qx-section-alt">
    <div class="qx-container qx-prose">
      <h2>What "AI" doesn't mean here</h2>
      <p>
        It doesn't place a trade without you. It doesn't guarantee an
        outcome. It reads current conditions and suggests a starting
        setup, the actual strategy still runs on the plain rules described
        on the <a href="/learn">Learn</a> page, Grid works a range, DCA
        buys on schedule, Momentum follows a confirmed trend. The AI's job
        ends at "here's a reasonable place to start", the strategy takes
        it from there.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="qx-cta">
    <div class="qx-container qx-cta-inner">
      <div>
        <h2>See it on a real pair</h2>
        <p>Start the bot creation wizard and try the AI Strategies tab for yourself.</p>
        <a class="qx-btn-primary qx-btn-lg" href={`${APP_URL}/signup`}>Trade Now</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .qx-ai-hero {
    padding: var(--space-48) 0 var(--space-24);
  }
  .qx-eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-data);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--teal-base);
    background: var(--teal-pale);
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-8);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-16);
  }
  .qx-ai-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4.5vw, 48px);
    color: var(--ink-base);
    max-width: 22ch;
  }
  .qx-lead {
    margin-top: var(--space-16);
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 58ch;
  }

  .qx-section {
    padding: var(--space-48) 0;
  }
  .qx-section-alt {
    background: var(--cream-deep);
  }

  .qx-cta {
    padding: var(--space-48) 0 var(--space-32);
  }
  .qx-cta-inner {
    background: var(--teal-deep);
    border-radius: var(--radius-2xl);
    padding: var(--space-48);
    text-align: center;
  }
  .qx-cta-inner h2 {
    color: var(--on-accent);
  }
  .qx-cta-inner p {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    color: var(--teal-sage);
    max-width: 48ch;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }
  .qx-cta-inner .qx-btn-primary {
    margin-top: var(--space-16);
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .qx-container {
      padding: 0 var(--space-16);
    }
    .qx-ai-hero {
      padding: var(--space-32) 0 var(--space-16);
    }
    .qx-ai-hero h1 {
      font-size: 26px;
    }
    .qx-lead {
      font-size: 16px;
    }
    .qx-section {
      padding: var(--space-32) 0;
    }
    .qx-cta-inner {
      padding: var(--space-32) var(--space-24);
    }
  }
</style>
